  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="0ebf-749e-71fe-52a3" name="Vikings (AoA2) - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF ANTIQUITY v2 #63 (unofficial, Martin Gibbins). Vikings- Scandinavian adventurers in search of loot or land- began to appear around the British Isles towards the end of the 8th Century. They terrorised coastal settlements and, in time, created settlements of their own, in Ireland, the Isles, Britain, France and what would become Russia. Most of these were eventually subsumed into the native culture, over which they held significant influence. Ironically the last Viking attacks on Britain were repulsed by the new Norman overlords – themselves descended from Viking settlers. Allies: The army may have allies from the Later Irish or Later Saxon Kingdoms lists.

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Vikings]
  Characters: up to 33%
  Infantry: at least 50%
  Special Troops and Allies: up to 33%
  Characters: Up to 33% Infantry: At least 50% Special Troops and Allies: Up to 33% The army list represents the Danish Great Army; if wishing to represent a raiding force then the Hirdmen may be fielded as Light Infantry.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
